Sources of self-efﬁcacy
Self-efﬁcacy theory postulates that people acquire information to evaluate efﬁcacy
beliefs from four primary sources: (a) enactive mastery experiences (actual
performances);

(b) observation of others (vicarious experiences);

(c) forms of
persuasion, both verbal and otherwise;

